{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01VRyCnxmU2XwNrc1Jtdgyg5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DZFfF3SzSJcQvyQxAEXRjq","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","old_string":"- **E3** — `get_cost_reduction` now also sums `spell_cost_reduction(game, spell)` from the\n  caster's battlefield permanents, only for instant/sorcery spells. Generic-only, clamped ≥0.","new_string":"- **E3** — `get_cost_reduction` now also sums `spell_cost_reduction(game, spell)` from the\n  caster's battlefield permanents, only for instant/sorcery spells. Generic-only, clamped ≥0.\n\n## sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic\n\n- **Exile-instead deviation from plan.** The plan suggested a `ReplacementEffect` setting\n  `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent.destination = \"exile\"`. But instant/sorcery spells\n  resolving go `STACK→GRAVEYARD` via `move_to_zone` with no replacement_event, and\n  `move_to_zone` only consults replacements when *leaving the battlefield* — so that path\n  can never fire for a resolving spell. Deviation: `_resolve_spell` now reads a card flag\n  `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` at the one resolve point and routes to exile. Deliberate\n  card-local limitation: covers the resolve-to-graveyard case (the normal one), not e.g.\n  the spell being countered.\n- **Fired `AttacksTriggeredEvent`.** Like `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (E1), this event class\n  existed but was *never fired* by the engine, so the documented attack-trigger seam (also\n  relied on by FDN Etali/Drakuseth) was dormant. Added a minimal additive fire in\n  `combat.declare_attackers_step`, once per declared attacker."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":298,"cache_read_input_tokens":174242,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":298},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a75e57b-d845-4814-b1a9-adfaef121449","uuid":"c031629c-ab9f-4526-b39a-8d67c8068c6e","request_id":"req_011CbtSBTKADZvDpB5kXhLSE"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DZFfF3SzSJcQvyQxAEXRjq","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a75e57b-d845-4814-b1a9-adfaef121449","uuid":"7a553ae0-9ebb-46c3-88cd-82782c1a35f2","timestamp":"2026-06-09T21:58:16.025Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"- **E3** — `get_cost_reduction` now also sums `spell_cost_reduction(game, spell)` from the\n  caster's battlefield permanents, only for instant/sorcery spells. Generic-only, clamped ≥0.","newString":"- **E3** — `get_cost_reduction` now also sums `spell_cost_reduction(game, spell)` from the\n  caster's battlefield permanents, only for instant/sorcery spells. Generic-only, clamped ≥0.\n\n## sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic\n\n- **Exile-instead deviation from plan.** The plan suggested a `ReplacementEffect` setting\n  `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent.destination = \"exile\"`. But instant/sorcery spells\n  resolving go `STACK→GRAVEYARD` via `move_to_zone` with no replacement_event, and\n  `move_to_zone` only consults replacements when *leaving the battlefield* — so that path\n  can never fire for a resolving spell. Deviation: `_resolve_spell` now reads a card flag\n  `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` at the one resolve point and routes to exile. Deliberate\n  card-local limitation: covers the resolve-to-graveyard case (the normal one), not e.g.\n  the spell being countered.\n- **Fired `AttacksTriggeredEvent`.** Like `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (E1), this event class\n  existed but was *never fired* by the engine, so the documented attack-trigger seam (also\n  relied on by FDN Etali/Drakuseth) was dormant. Added a minimal additive fire in\n  `combat.declare_attackers_step`, once per declared attacker.","originalFile":"# KEY_DECISIONS — SOS card implementation\n\nLightweight log of ambiguities, deviations, and deliberate card-local limitations.\n\n## Engine (E1–E3)\n\n- **E1** — Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` only in `cast_spell` (not `cast_spell_free`),\n  per the plan. Copies via `copy_spell` and free-casts do not re-fire it, which keeps\n  casualty/storm-style triggers from looping on free casts.\n- **E2** — Fired `BeginningOfPrecombatMainTriggeredEvent` from `GameState.advance_phase`\n  after `empty_mana_pools()`, so mana added by handlers survives into the main phase and\n  it behaves the same on direct `advance_to_phase` and in a real turn.\n- **E3** — `get_cost_reduction` now also sums `spell_cost_reduction(game, spell)` from the\n  caster's battlefield permanents, only for instant/sorcery spells. Generic-only, clamped ≥0.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":3,"newStart":12,"newLines":18,"lines":["   it behaves the same on direct `advance_to_phase` and in a real turn."," - **E3** — `get_cost_reduction` now also sums `spell_cost_reduction(game, spell)` from the","   caster's battlefield permanents, only for instant/sorcery spells. Generic-only, clamped ≥0.","+","+## sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic","+","+- **Exile-instead deviation from plan.** The plan suggested a `ReplacementEffect` setting","+  `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent.destination = \"exile\"`. But instant/sorcery spells","+  resolving go `STACK→GRAVEYARD` via `move_to_zone` with no replacement_event, and","+  `move_to_zone` only consults replacements when *leaving the battlefield* — so that path","+  can never fire for a resolving spell. Deviation: `_resolve_spell` now reads a card flag","+  `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` at the one resolve point and routes to exile. Deliberate","+  card-local limitation: covers the resolve-to-graveyard case (the normal one), not e.g.","+  the spell being countered.","+- **Fired `AttacksTriggeredEvent`.** Like `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` (E1), this event class","+  existed but was *never fired* by the engine, so the documented attack-trigger seam (also","+  relied on by FDN Etali/Drakuseth) was dormant. Added a minimal additive fire in","+  `combat.declare_attackers_step`, once per declared attacker."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
